WEBVTT

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:11.460
Anyone but the keeper using both hands...

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.470
Holding the ball underwater...

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:17.350
Hitting it in the air...

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:23.640
Not shooting within 30 seconds
of your team getting the ball...

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.350
All of these are fouls,
and your team loses the ball.

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:28.650
"Foul"

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:28.650
All of these are fouls,
and your team loses the ball.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:29.940
"Foul"

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:29.940
Oh?

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:35.530
Impeding someone without
the ball is also another foul.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:40.410
But attacking whoever holds it
is allowed by the rules.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:41.490
Attacking?

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:49.040
Yeah. Grabbing their arms, pulling...
Some players go further than that.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.550
What?!

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.880
Hence, "water wrestling"!

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:56.720
The referee only calls fouls
they're able to see.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:02.220
It's important to learn what you
can get away with underwater.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.680
Seriously?

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.730
He wasn't lying!

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:10.190
Who knew grade-schoolers
were this aggressive?!

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.240
He's got my wrist!

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.910
Ours!

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:23.910
Crap!

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.170
Go!

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:44.060
--Here they come!
--Defense!

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:04.660
Well, well.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:12.290
Why didn't you move away?
Your defender came over to me.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:13.290
Sorry.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:18.260
And what about you?!
Why didn't you pass to Minato?!

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:23.300
It wouldn't accomplish much.
He'd let the ball get stolen.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.020
"Yamanami High School"
"Mizushima Junior Team"     "2"

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:31.060
Oh, is that right?

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:36.860
Then how about I take a shot?!

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:54.670
"Kurashiki Community Pool"

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:56.670
"Yamanami High School"
"Mizushima Junior Team"    "5" "6" "3" "4"

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:41.610
"Episode 5: Dude, That's Scary!!!"

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:44.990
"Episode 5: Dude, That's Scary!!!"
We've got this! Our first victory!

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:46.820
"Episode 5: Dude, That's Scary!!!"
Don't let one victory go to your head.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:48.160
Don't let one victory go to your head.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:50.990
It wasn't even us who won.

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:53.620
Something wrong?

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:56.370
He's worse than I imagined.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:58.630
Oh, Kiyomizu?

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:00.090
You know him?

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:02.550
Yeah, a little.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:03.840
Hmm?

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:06.340
Whoa, whoa, back it up!

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:11.180
Why didn't you pass when
I was open, you ball hog?!

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:14.310
Let's break it up, okay?

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:22.980
The player covering Babayaro
was between you two.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:29.570
A pass would probably get intercepted,
so I chose the better strategy.

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:35.410
Yeah, well, you ignored our strategy
of getting the ball to Minato.

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:36.460
That's because--

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:39.130
It's my fault! Sorry!

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:46.260
I couldn't do a damn thing.
Sorry for ruining the strategy.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:51.430
It's my bad, too. I should've
changed the strategy, but no...

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:53.770
I only held us back.

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:55.390
Likewise.

00:05:55.390 --> 00:06:00.270
Well, I'm better than I thought.
And Amiami's swimming is sick.

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:04.980
Still, with Minato as he is,
we can't beat my brother.

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:06.990
Let's hope you progress.

00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:08.910
Right.

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:10.570
Sorry.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:14.580
I'm going ahead.

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:16.160
Got plans?

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:22.710
No, but I need time to think
if I wanna keep playing or not.

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:23.920
Hey!

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:31.050
Internal strife!

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:33.220
Let's get outta here.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:36.060
What's his problem?

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:40.190
We just lost to grade-schoolers?

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:42.060
You think he'll quit?

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:43.770
Beats me.

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:48.030
We can't compete with six.
Let's find someone new.

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:51.610
Are you kidding me?!
He hasn't quit just yet!

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:53.910
Relax, relax.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:58.830
Thank you!

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:03.290
This pouch is super cute!
Is it an original?

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:09.670
You okay?

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:15.100
Welcome home! How was it?

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:18.430
You had a match, right?

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:21.140
Yeah, we got stomped.

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:32.410
I swallowed so much water, I could barf.

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:37.540
Man, I was totally useless.

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:49.960
Dammit! Dammit!

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:54.050
I'm pathetic.

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:59.270
Was I really a prodigy?

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:14.360
Big Bro! Big Bro!

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:16.620
Hey, Big Bro!

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:19.950
Huh? I fell asleep?

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:21.960
Hey.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.620
Someone's here from your club.

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:25.960
Huh?

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:31.760
Sorry for dropping in.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:33.430
Yeah? What's up?

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:37.680
Um... Can we talk outside?

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.220
Sure.

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:06.080
Sure is a pretty view.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:10.630
Isn't it? I've loved coming here
since I was little.

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:15.430
Um...

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:16.470
Hmm?

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:19.550
Don't you want your memories back?

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:20.470
Huh?

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:25.850
You can't remember people
you've met. Isn't that scary?

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:30.650
I'm getting treatment, but no luck so far.

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:38.030
But I consider myself lucky
for getting to see this view.

00:09:38.030 --> 00:09:41.200
Oh, yeah. By the way...

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:46.410
You said Asumi told you
that I was out of the hospital?

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:47.620
Yeah...

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:52.210
It didn't seem like she recognized you.

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:55.470
Sorry, I lied.

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:57.180
What?

00:09:57.180 --> 00:10:04.560
I've never met her. I heard from
my little sister in Asumi's grade.

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:05.930
Oh...

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:09.150
I've told lots of other lies, too.

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:10.360
Huh?

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:12.110
I came to tell you.

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:13.070
Wh-What?

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:17.030
First off, you and I were never close.

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:18.780
Huh?

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:22.990
It's just that, in junior high,
I admired you.

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:27.210
I was always too nervous
to even talk to you.

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:31.250
What about making me
laugh with "taxicrab"?

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:35.920
The only time I ever spoke
to you was that once.

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:37.170
Ah...

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:45.520
But when I heard from Momo-<i>senpai</i>
that you woke up but forgot your past...

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:47.600
He doesn't remember?

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:48.690
Nope.

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:52.150
He had no reaction when he saw us.

00:10:55.190 --> 00:11:00.570
So... I pretended to be
your pal to get close to you.

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:01.610
Huh?!

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:05.950
I got to know you to see
if you really forgot.

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:11.420
Dude, that's scary! Sorry,
but it is! Why even do that?!

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:16.000
I figured, with you,
any team would be strong!

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:21.090
I was benched for all
three years of junior high.

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:22.470
Eh?

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:25.680
I never played in an official game.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:31.480
I thought I'd get to in my third year,
but a second year took the spot.

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:35.940
Shogaku has combined grades,
so graduating wouldn't help.

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:39.900
Once I realized I'd never be
a regular member...

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:46.450
"I'd get to play on a weak team...
Oh! If we had Minato, we'd be strong!"

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:51.370
I thought, "I'll show those
guys up real good!"

00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:59.260
I ran away from my teammates.

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:06.510
But it didn't go as planned.
And you even warned me.

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:07.560
Huh?

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:11.140
"Can you not get your hopes up?"

00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:16.820
I figured you were just being
modest, but after today...

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:21.700
"Oh, he's serious.
This isn't the Minato I know."

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:26.450
It finally sank in that
you lost your talent...

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:33.670
I thought I couldn't compete
with you on a genetic level.

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:43.130
"He's too good! How does he do that?!
This freak can't possibly be human!"

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:44.050
"Freak"?

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:49.220
So, to think I'd see you
play that poorly...

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:52.890
I'm sorry if I've been rude,

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:58.570
but it's tough seeing someone
you admired like that.

00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:00.780
I'm quitting water polo.

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:02.280
Eh?

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:04.320
I'll announce it Monday.

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:05.490
Uh--!

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:20.130
I wonder if Ei will really quit.
Just when it was getting fun...

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:22.840
"Water Polo"

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:28.350
Something wrong?

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:32.310
It's nothing.

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:28.030
Is that all you've got?!

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:29.700
No!

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:31.320
Then show me!

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:32.740
Okay!

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:47.130
Take ten minutes.

00:14:47.130 --> 00:14:48.550
Okay!

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:02.060
Hey, Kiyomizu!

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:08.280
Um, hello.

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:14.780
I see. It's like you've forgotten.

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:16.410
Yeah.

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:18.330
That's rough.

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:19.370
Yeah.

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:24.090
So, who are you here for? Momo? Keita?

00:15:24.090 --> 00:15:27.340
Uh, no... You.

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:34.510
I have a question.
What made me so amazing before?

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:40.480
I just can't imagine myself
being the best in Japan.

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:44.060
What sort of strengths did I have?

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:50.860
Your strength was the wide range
of motion in your shoulder blades.

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:52.530
Shoulder blades...

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:56.080
But where you excelled
more than anyone...

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:03.210
Where are they?

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:04.750
Where?!

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:24.100
Hey, be careful!
You'll never make it, so cut it out!

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:42.790
Babi, let's head to club.

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:44.750
Y-Yeah!

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:55.970
Let's head to club.

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:57.350
Yeah.

00:17:02.890 --> 00:17:04.810
"Resignation"

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:08.940
Got a sec?

00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:15.450
Huh?

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:20.910
Huh?! What the hell?! In dramas,
the roof is always unlocked!

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:23.960
I wanted to talk somewhere open!

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:28.170
What's this about?
I've already decided to quit.

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:30.000
Uh, yeah.

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:36.720
I thought I'd tell you
a decision of my own.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:39.890
Yesterday, I met Advisor Bizen.

00:17:41.310 --> 00:17:44.640
When I asked him my strengths...

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:49.980
Where you excelled more than
anyone was putting in effort.

00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:52.570
So he said. And...

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:57.160
I believe you had DVDs
in your room. Watch 'em.

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:57.910
He said.

00:17:57.910 --> 00:17:59.740
What was on video?

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:02.490
Well, you see...!

00:18:02.490 --> 00:18:05.580
Just me practicing my shooting form.

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:06.410
Huh?

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:11.540
Over and over. Thirty minutes every day.

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:14.960
You made every effort you possibly could.

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:20.140
You practiced at home, at school,
and even recorded your form.

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:26.100
You studied the videos before bed
and practiced passing against the wall.

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:29.600
"Modern Water Polo Handbook"
"Water Polo Rules Book"

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:29.600
To strategize, you studied old books
to see why rules had changed.

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:32.320
"Remain"

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:32.320
"One type of rule violation in water polo."
To strategize, you studied old books
to see why rules had changed.

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:37.490
You wanted to learn how
strategies had evolved.

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:40.660
Very few people go that far.

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:45.500
Your greatest talent was all your effort.

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:51.710
He said. I found a ball in my closet,
but it's as smooth as can be!

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:58.510
The grippy texture is worn completely off!
I must've trained like crazy!

00:18:58.510 --> 00:19:03.470
I wasn't a prodigy.
I just worked incredibly hard!

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:12.810
Step by step, I climbed up to the
wonderful place known as best in Japan.

00:19:12.810 --> 00:19:15.610
It's the result of training day after day,

00:19:15.610 --> 00:19:21.910
building upon myself
until I finally could do it.

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:26.370
You made it up? Way to go, Kamekichi!

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:32.920
You thought I was different
on a genetic level, but I'm not.

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:34.960
And what a relief!

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:36.340
Huh?

00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:42.140
I'm so bad, I thought
I lost my gift for it.

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:46.850
But if I never had it,
I can work to get good again!

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:53.610
The me of the past is my rival!
I'll do all I can to beat who I once was!

00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:58.360
So... will you keep playing water polo?

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:03.740
It'll be reassuring to have you,
who knew me in the past.

00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:07.830
You know all about water polo,
so maybe you can teach me?

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:12.580
I promise, I'll make you admire me again!

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:18.670
You'll forgive me?
I said mean things, Minato.

00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:22.720
Not much to forgive.
It's true that I'm bad.

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:27.430
But I'm selfish and scheming.
You're fine with that?

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:34.020
Yeah, I can tell. You sneakily
stopped calling me "Senpai."

00:20:34.020 --> 00:20:37.190
Either way, I think you're interesting.

00:20:53.790 --> 00:20:55.580
Go change already!

00:20:55.580 --> 00:21:00.840
I'm telling you, practice is pointless
if Eitaro quits since--

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:03.010
We don't know if he's quitting!

00:21:03.010 --> 00:21:05.260
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:21:18.690 --> 00:21:23.900
Sorry I'm late! My stomach was acting up!

00:21:23.900 --> 00:21:25.700
Me, too.

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:28.320
Uh, yeah. Sure.

00:21:28.320 --> 00:21:29.910
I'll go change!

00:21:29.910 --> 00:21:31.830
Me, too!

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:33.710
Are we safe?

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:35.420
Think so.

00:21:52.020 --> 00:21:57.650
One, two, three, four, five,
six, seven, eight...!

00:21:57.650 --> 00:22:03.280
Two, two, three,
four, five, six, seven...!

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:10.740
Chinu! About practice...

00:22:10.740 --> 00:22:13.080
Y-Yeah!

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:17.960
All right! Let's practice long
passes today! Pair up!

00:22:17.960 --> 00:22:19.000
Okay!

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:20.170
Um...

00:22:20.170 --> 00:22:23.460
Um! Mind if we pair up?!

00:22:23.460 --> 00:22:24.420
Sure!

00:22:24.420 --> 00:22:27.760
Okay! I'll grab us a ball, Minato-<i>senpai</i>!

00:22:27.760 --> 00:22:31.680
<i>Just who are they</i>

00:22:34.020 --> 00:22:39.150
<i>There's a me just like me at my side</i>

00:22:39.150 --> 00:22:42.150
<i>Laughing</i>

00:22:46.400 --> 00:22:49.740
<i>All the many sights and</i>

00:22:49.740 --> 00:22:53.200
<i>All the words you left behind</i>

00:22:53.200 --> 00:23:00.000
<i>Are looking a little warped</i>

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:03.420
<i>Someone, anyone tell me</i>

00:23:03.420 --> 00:23:06.380
<i>It hurts, it hurts, it hurts</i>

00:23:06.380 --> 00:23:14.720
<i>What am I suddenly crying for?</i>
